      "role": "user",
      "content": "not bad, the vibe is definitely there. i like the bit about the 'slow hunger'.\n\nbut i just ran it through the internal tool and the depth score is coming back super low because of the word count. the devs are saying if the score stays this low, the quest might not even trigger in the current build because the engine thinks it's a 'micro-interaction' rather than a full quest. \n\ncan you expand on this a bit? maybe add some more lore about the Old Void or the history of the Hollow? and again, i'm serious—don't just repeat yourself or use filler words to make it longer. i need actual substance, just... more of it. we need to get that score up so it actually passes the check.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
